Subject: [PATCH 0/2] drm/panel: samsung: add EA8074

This adds a driver for the Samsung EA8074 command mode AMOLED panel
(1080x2244) found in the Xiaomi Mi 8 SE (xiaomi-sirius, SDM710), together
with its device tree binding.

The panel is driven through the SDM710 DSI host in command mode. The mode,
lane count, reset waveform, supply order and delays, on/off command arrays
and the brightness encoding all come from the panel's vendor device tree and
driver at SDM710-Development/android_kernel_xiaomi_sdm710@06a01bad; the
kernel API usage follows panel-samsung-ams639rq08.c, a command mode AMOLED
panel on the same DSI host. Nothing was guessed and nothing was taken from a
different panel.

The series has been built and run: it compiles against a pinned tree, its
binding passes dt_binding_check and dtbs_check, checkpatch reports no errors
or warnings, and the resulting image was booted on the device, where the
panel comes up and displays.

One deviation from the vendor command arrays is deliberate and is stated in
the driver and in patch 2's commit message rather than hidden: 13 records
use DCS long write (0x39) with a two-byte payload, and the exported helper
derives the data type from the buffer length, so those are sent as 0x15
short-write-with-parameter with the same command and parameter. Whether the
panel accepts 0x15 there is not verified. Closing it needs either hardware
confirmation or a typed-DCS helper in the DRM core, which is a separate
change and is not part of this series.

